{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTAZ4DNFDTaPqoBrKfRG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added citations for the headline comparator and the commute-time background, but three of the five targeted references could not be retrieved. The paper compiles to 11 pages with no undefined citations. Claim validation passes (19 claims), and the scientific-evidence report shows zero dangling references. I couldn't run `validate_figures.py` (import error) or the `compile_latex.sh` wrapper (`pdftotext` missing), so I compiled with `pdflatex`/`bibtex` directly. The figures were not touched.\n\n**Added to `references.bib` and `references_provenance.json`** (all found through Semantic Scholar):\n- **Aleliunas et al. 1979:** source of the 2m(n−1) bound. It is now cited in the Introduction and in Related Work (worst-case bounds).\n- **Lovász survey:** cited for the hitting-time and commute-time machinery. Semantic Scholar's record is dated 2001, not the original 1993 version, so the year in the bibliography is the retrieved one. I gave it an ASCII key, `Lovasz2001RandomWO`.\n- **Doyle and Snell, *Random Walks and Electrical Networks*:** cited in Related Work and in the Discussion and Conclusion for the commute-time/effective-resistance link. This was not on the gap list; it was the closest retrievable source for that point.\n\n**Not retrievable, so not cited:**\n- **Chandra et al. and the Matthews bound:** I removed the \"Matthews-type bounds\" attribution in the Discussion and reworded the resistance-features sentence around the commute-time/resistance relation, citing Doyle–Snell and Lovász. The Supplementary note still names the unscored \"Matthews-style\" candidate, but only as that candidate's label.\n- **Hoerl–Kennard ridge regression:** the ridge passages stay uncited, which matches the paper's claim of no novelty for the model class.\n\nI added two entries to `claims_grounding.json` covering the new citations. I also logged the decisions in `memory.md`, but not in the campaign-level memory, because `global_memory` points to `../investigation`, which doesn't exist here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":62026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":544,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":708,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bd783da-1739-49a5-a1ff-6fbbac76c044","uuid":"35d9a3ab-2756-4a19-a44b-5a03fe4f226f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:50:41.382Z","request_id":"req_011CgTAZ3edFuCKY591ZuhN3"}
